course: dictionary
lesson: 12531
title: Despondency: a heavy heart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Despondency is a noun, a naming word for a feeling. It means low spirits and lost hope, when you are so sad that you do not want to try. The describing word is despondent, as in «She felt despondent.»
explain: Use the clues around the word. «After the team lost every match, Sam sat alone with a face of despondency.» Sam lost, he sits alone and his face looks sad, so despondency must be a deep sadness where hope has gone. Test it: sadness fits the sentence, but despondency is stronger, because it includes giving up.
explain: Despondency often grows slowly. «Her despondency grew each day that the letter did not come.» Waiting day after day with no news shows hope fading. A bad mood lasts an afternoon, but despondency can last much longer.
fact: Despondency is a noun, so it names a feeling. You do not usually say "a despondency".
fact: «Despondency» means low spirits and lost hope, being very sad and unwilling to try.
fact: «Despondent» is the describing word: «She felt despondent after the test.»
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad sinks into deep despondency in his dungeon until the gaoler's daughter cheers him up.
fact: In The Pilgrim's Progress, Christian falls into the «Slough of Despond», a bog of despair.
exercise: «After the team lost every match, Sam sat alone with a face of despondency.» What does despondency mean? | Feeling hungry after a long day | A kind of weather, like fog | Loud excitement after a win | *Deep sadness with lost hope
exercise: What kind of word is despondency? | A verb, a doing word | A joining word | An adjective, a describing word | *A noun, a naming word for a feeling
exercise: «Her despondency grew each day that the letter did not come.» Which clue shows hope is fading? | Her name was written on the envelope | *Each day the letter did not come | The sun was shining outside | She bought a new hat
test: Toad sinks into despondency in his dungeon. What helps him? | The sun comes out | He is sent to bed early | *The gaoler's daughter cheers him up | Stories about the river
test: Why can talking to someone help fight despondency? | Talking is never useful for feelings | It means you must be alone | *It reminds you that hope is not lost and that others care | Talking makes you tired, so you stop feeling sad
exam: Which sentence uses despondency correctly? | Despondency is a fast, bouncy game | The despondency of the red bicycle was loud | The class had despondency about the maths trip | *After he failed the test, Ben sank into despondency and stopped trying
